          "$deleted": true,
          "class": "Illusionist",
          "cost": "20",
          "description": "",
          "duration": "Instantaneous",
          "roll": "",
          "spell_name": "Detonate Phantasm",
          "target": "One creature"
        },
        "2": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "class": "Illusionist",
          "cost": "20",
          "description": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">When another creature is threatened by an attack, spell, or other danger,<br>command one Phantasm to take their place.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Any Checks that are part of the danger will be performed against the Phantasm.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">The Phantasm shields the creature, suffering an amount of damage corresponding to how much PV it has left, until it shatters.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">The remaining damage goes to the creature being defended. </span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">All status effects related to the attack are nullified</span></p>",
          "duration": "Instantaneous",
          "roll": "",
          "spell_name": "Illusory Shield",
          "target": "One creature"
        },
        "3": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "class": "Arcanist",
          "cost": "30",
          "description": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">You may use an action and spend 30 Mind Points to </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">summon </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">the power of one of the Arcana you have previously bound.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><strong>MERGING WITH AN ARCANUM</strong><br></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">When you summon an Arcanum, you gain their </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">merge </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">benefits; those benefits last until the Arcanum is dismissed You cannot summon an Arcanum while already merged with one; you must first dismiss the current Arcanum.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>DISMISSING AN ARCANUM</strong><br>If you are merged with an Arcanum, they will be automatically dismissed at the end of the scene, if you die or fall unconscious, or if you leave the scene.<br>You may also willingly dismiss the Arcanum you are currently merged with: <strong>this never requires an action</strong>, but during a conflict it can only be done on your turn, and never while another effect is being resolved.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">When you willingly dismiss an Arcanum, you may use their dismiss effect - if the Arcanum is dismissed for any other reason, this effect cannot be used. </span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">You are also free to ignore a dismiss effect if you don't want to use it.<br>If a pulse or dismiss effect deals damage, it will deal 5 extra damage if you are level 20 or higher, or 10 extra damage if you are level 40 or higher.</span></p>",
          "duration": "Scene",
          "roll": "",
          "spell_name": "Summon Arcanum",
          "target": "Self"
        }
      },
      "notes_text": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Phantasms rules.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><br>1. Phantasms are entities of pure energy, capable of taking on various sizes and forms — even becoming exact replicas of you!<br>2. They </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">do not talk or have a mind of their own</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">, and are </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">not capable of reason or logic</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">.<br>3. They only follow </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">simple one-clause </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">commands and cannot abstract meaning or extrapolate from them. For example, if you ask a Phantasm to<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;grab some milk, it knows where the milk is because you do. It also knows that you are feeling thirsty — because you know it too. However, it won't<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;understand that milk can quench thirst, nor will it know to pour the milk into a glass; these thought processes are </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">too complex </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">for Phantasms. So,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;it would just bring you the whole bottle of milk, with a deadpan look.<br>4. Phantasms share your base Attributes and Defenses, have no MP, and their </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Phantasmal Vitality </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">(PV) is equal to your </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">base Insight die size plus<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;your level (= 25)</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">. They have Immunity to all status effects.<br>5. They have no Initiative score. Phantasms do not get a turn during conflicts, but </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">on your turn, you can perform an action to command one or more Phantasms, depending on the wording of the spell</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">. </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Phantasms always target Magical Defense.<br>6. You may create a Phantasm and command it </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">in the same action</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">. After this first command — which directly follows its creation — on your next turn, it requires </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">a whole action to be commanded again</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">. Therefore, you cannot command Phantasm 1 and then proceed to create Phantasm 2 in the same&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;action.<br>7. Unless stated otherwise, you can have up to </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">3 </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Phantasms active at the same time. Attempts to cast more Phantasms beyond 3 will fail.<br>8. Your Phantasms shatter if they fall to 0 PV, if you fall to 0 HP, or if you leave the scene. You can also shatter them through skills, spells, or at will.</span></p>",
